--
-- A corpus is the node programs by role: for each role a machine (a state type with a view over
-- the node signature), its initial state, the wire form of its messages, and what the process
-- leaves with when the machine stops. A configuration is a value: the platform, and per node
-- its role and its address (the list is the wiring: a node's peers are the others' addresses).
-- deploy corpus config is the fleet: the behaviour by node id and the initial state (what
-- lib/fleet.cub's properties are stated of), and for each node the process that runs on its
-- box — the machine's process handled into Linux commands over UDP (net-on-linux) and those
-- into the drivers' signature W (linux-run), a Step W that #build writes as a binary.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- handlers at any level
-- lib/proc.cub's handle with the level free: the node's process is interpreted into Linux, and
-- that into W, so the first interpretation is at the level above
import "library.cub"
import "net.cub"
import "fleet.cub"
